  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The yak coat is created by working "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "loop-stitch-yk"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "loop stitch"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " on every alternate round across both the body and the lower head. Cut the loops after completion to create a shaggy fleece texture. All pieces start with a "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "magic-ring-yk"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "magic ring"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Yarn and yarn amounts"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "You need approx. 54 g of dark brown DK. Use a second long-fibre yarn in a matching shade for the loop stitches if you want a shaggier texture. Stuff each piece with firm stuffing before closing."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Head"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Work a 8 cm by 10 cm oval head (23 rounds). Work "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "loop-stitch-yk"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "loop stitches"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " on every other round from round 3 to round 14. Fit "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "safety-eyes-yk"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "safety eyes"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " at round 10."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Horns (make 2)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Work a 1.5 cm base cone over 5 cm (14 rounds). Use "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "dc2tog-yk"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "dc2tog"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " to taper to a point. Stuff lightly. Sew to the head above the ears, curving outward and slightly forward."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Body"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Work a 11 cm by 14 cm oval body (32 rounds). Work loop stitches on every other round across the full body. Stuff firmly."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Legs (make 4)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Work a 3.5 cm diameter by 5 cm capsule per leg (11 rounds). Work loop stitches on the upper half of each leg. Stuff firmly."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Assembly"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Sew head to the front end of the body using "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "ladder-stitch-yk"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "ladder stitch"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ". Pin legs to the body base and check the yak stands level before sewing. Cut all loops after assembly for the finished shaggy look."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What to try next"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The amigurumi bison uses a similar large oval head without the shaggy coat technique."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}